  "text": "In this spring, most of us read from one page. In April 2014, 49 of us said \"the save american,\" 48 of us said \"the save american workers,\" and 42 of us said \"the save american workers act,\" each peaking on the same day, 2014-04-03. Alongside it, 29 of us carried \"2575 the save,\" 28 of us \"2575 the save american,\" and 27 of us \"2575 the save american workers\" — the bill number and the name moving together, first recorded from Todd Young in 2013. Twenty-seven of us said \"path to prosperity,\" peaking 2014-04-10. Later that month, on 2014-04-30, 26 of us turned to \"military construction and veterans affairs.\" We did not vary the wording; we repeated it. That is the record of what we chose to say together this month, and how many of us said it.",
